5 10  ; 5-10 years
3701

BEGINTEXT

 East vs. West     An intermediate scenario for 1 to 2 players

 by Edward Masterson, George Moromisato, and David Margil

 This scenario simulates a classic military confrontation: superior tech-    
 nology against overwhelming numbers. Player 1, controlling the eastern
 empire, has a small number of advanced ships (penetrators and starships) 
 while player 2, the western empire, has a large force of jumpships and 
 hunter-killers. Unlike other scenarios, the emphasis here is on battle 
 tactics, not on economic and political maneuvering.

 Victory Conditions (see World/Close Up of your capital):
  
 Complete: You will be declared the winner if on a given turn you hold
 either the capital of your opponent, or FOUR of his or her worlds.

 Partial: You will win a partial victory if on the 15th year you hold all
 of your worlds and TWO of your opponent's worlds.

 No Victory: If no one has won by the 15th year, the game is a draw.
NEWPAGE
ENDTEXT

